[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"314","stub":{"id":"314","section":"1. Tangle Blue Creek to Clair Engle Lake","altname":"","river":"Trinity","difficulty":"IIItoIV","states":["USA-CAL"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"209","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"112844","location":{"latitude":"41.2264","longitude":"-122.644"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"118125","location":{"latitude":"41.0632","longitude":"-122.7"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"13.6","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"m9GfsagO8jqPVebzMVlGf","ext":"jpg","post_id":"5SgABiXJT0AIqHYdSvPDV","description":"","caption":"First part of Bear Creek Rapid","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Robin Levick","poi_id":"r2D932zDLzv1hruQwcQMU","photo_date":"2024-04-21T21:21:29.000Z","updated_at":"2024-04-22T21:21:29.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/m9GfsagO8jqPVebzMVlGf","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/m9GfsagO8jqPVebzMVlGf"}}],"detail":{"id":"314","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"This is an absolute classic. It doesn't run every year, and often runs for a short time, but is worth the drive if you can catch it.\n\nThe section above this run was clearly runnable and is roadside, if anyone has beta on it please add the run here on AW.\n\nThe run is absolutely continuous class III with one class IV at Bear Creek. Swims can be painful as the river isn't particularly deep and one gets pinballed at best and pinned at worst.\n\nAt 1300cfs there's some scraping for the first mile, so I imagine 800cfs would be pretty bony. 1500 is a great level. River should go above 2000 but would definitely become a class IV due to the continuous nature.\n\nThe class IV Bear Creek rapid about 1/3 of the way through the run. It has two defined sections of whitewater with a small swift recovery section in between. The first part can be seen from the road, but just a bit down the road from there there you can drive off of the highwauy onto a dirt road into the trees to see the lower part of the rapid. It's advised to scout this on the way to the put-in, as the lower part is hard to scout from the riverbank.","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"13.8","correlations":[{"reachID":"314","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"800","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"2000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"TRINITY R AB COFFEE C NR TRINITY CENTER CA","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"11523200","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"209","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"3.85","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"41.11122108","longitude":"-122.7055474"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/11523200","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/11523200/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":"Previous Flowbands: \nRange of Boatable Flows (R0-R9): 800 - 2000 cfs  Comment: Actual boatable range unknown to this author.\n\nMigration Errors: \nSingle range is valid but doesn't provide low/medium/high runnable\nThere is one comment for all of low/medium/high runnable.","comment":null,"status":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"va